","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0812":{"code":"F-0812","title":"Procure food from sources approved or considered satisfactory and store, prepare, distribute and serve food in accordance with professional standards.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"food_nutrition","concept_label":"Food, nutrition & hydration"},"cms-f0880":{"code":"F-0880","title":"Provide and implement an infection prevention and control program.","category":"Infection Control Deficiencies","concept":"infection_prevention","concept_label":"Infection prevention"},"cms-f0550":{"code":"F-0550","title":"Honor the resident's right to a dignified existence, self-determination, communication, and to exercise his or her rights.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0641":{"code":"F-0641","title":"Ensure each resident receives an accurate assessment.","category":"Resident Assessment and Care Planning Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0688":{"code":"F-0688","title":"Provide appropriate care for a resident to maintain and/or improve range of motion (ROM), limited ROM and/or mobility, unless a decline is for a medical reason.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0690":{"code":"F-0690","title":"Provide appropriate care for residents who are continent or incontinent of bowel/bladder, appropriate catheter care,  and appropriate care  to prevent urinary tract infections.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0700":{"code":"F-0700","title":"Try different approaches before using a bed rail.  If a bed rail is needed, the facility must (1) assess a resident for safety risk; (2) review these risks and benefits with the resident/representative; (3) get informed consent; and (4) Correctly install and maintain the bed rail.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0803":{"code":"F-0803","title":"Ensure menus must meet the nutritional needs of residents, be prepared in advance, be followed, be updated, be reviewed by dietician, and meet the needs of the resident.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"food_nutrition","concept_label":"Food, nutrition & hydration"},"cms-f0909":{"code":"F-0909","title":"Regularly inspect all bed frames, mattresses, and bed rails (if any) for safety; and all bed rails and mattresses must attach safely to the bed frame.","category":"Environmental Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-f0609":{"code":"F-0609","title":"Timely report suspected abuse, neglect, or theft and report the results of the investigation to proper authorities.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0607":{"code":"F-0607","title":"Develop and implement policies and procedures to prevent abuse, neglect, and theft.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-k0291":{"code":"K-0291","title":"Install emergency lighting that can last at least 1 1/2 hours.","category":"Egress Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-k0293":{"code":"K-0293","title":"Have properly located and lighted \"Exit\" signs.","category":"Egress Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-k0912":{"code":"K-0912","title":"Have power receptacles that are properly grounded.","category":"Gas, Vacuum, and Electrical Systems Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-f0578":{"code":"F-0578","title":"Honor the resident's right to request, refuse, and/or discontinue treatment, to participate in or refuse to participate in experimental research, and to formulate an advance directive.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0657":{"code":"F-0657","title":"Develop the complete care plan within 7 days of the comprehensive assessment; and prepared, reviewed, and revised by a team of health professionals.","category":"Resident Assessment and Care Planning Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0677":{"code":"F-0677","title":"Provide care and assistance to perform activities of daily living for any resident who is unable.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0686":{"code":"F-0686","title":"Provide appropriate pressure ulcer care and prevent new ulcers from developing.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0725":{"code":"F-0725","title":"Provide enough nursing staff every day to meet the needs of every resident; and have a licensed nurse in charge on each shift.","category":"Nursing and Physician Services Deficiencies","concept":"staffing","concept_label":"Staffing & supervision"},"cms-f0757":{"code":"F-0757","title":"Ensure each resident’s drug regimen must be free from unnecessary drugs.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0758":{"code":"F-0758","title":"Implement gradual dose reductions(GDR) and non-pharmacological interventions, unless contraindicated, prior to initiating or instead of continuing psychotropic medication; and PRN orders for psychotropic medications are only used when the medication is necessary and PRN use is limited.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0761":{"code":"F-0761","title":"Ensure drugs and biologicals used in the facility are labeled in accordance with currently accepted professional principles; and all drugs and biologicals must be stored in locked compartments, separately locked, compartments for controlled drugs.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0802":{"code":"F-0802","title":"Provide sufficient support personnel to safely and effectively carry out the functions of the food and nutrition service.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"food_nutrition","concept_label":"Food, nutrition & hydration"},"cms-f0804":{"code":"F-0804","title":"Ensure food and drink is palatable, attractive, and at a safe and appetizing temperature.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"food_nutrition","concept_label":"Food, nutrition & hydration"},"cms-f0805":{"code":"F-0805","title":"Ensure each resident receives and the facility provides food prepared in a form designed to meet individual needs.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"food_nutrition","concept_label":"Food, nutrition & hydration"},"cms-f0552":{"code":"F-0552","title":"Ensure that residents are fully informed and understand their health status, care and treatments.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0637":{"code":"F-0637","title":"Assess the resident when there is a significant change in condition","category":"Resident Assessment and Care Planning Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0644":{"code":"F-0644","title":"Coordinate assessments with the pre-admission screening and resident review program; and referring for services as needed.","category":"Resident Assessment and Care Planning Deficien